{"author":{"id":"1d5f412cdeafe9987ad9876b0995bf5032718543d34c038a50cdb41808e9874c"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788305119,"nonce":"VB8cGErHcCgBbjLVL7NpGq+3Hcc=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOULVc1M8AAAABPPhb4g","github-url":"https://github.com/kanya-approve/torram-ng/issues/2","origin":"github"},"title":"start_offset uses a falsy check on a legitimately-zero value, and is assigned before the file guard","message":"In `guess_file()`:\n\n```python\nidx, file_offset = get_chunk(files_sizes_array, offset * piece_length)\nif not file_info.start_offset:\n    file_info.start_offset = file_offset\n\nif idx == file_idx:\n    ...\n```\n\nTwo bugs:\n\n1. `start_offset` is initialised to `None`, and `if not x` is true for both `None` **and** `0`. A genuine offset of 0 never sticks, so the assignment keeps firing.\n2. The assignment happens **before** the `if idx == file_idx:` guard, so `file_offset` is the offset within whatever file that piece happens to land in — not this file. It ends up holding the first non-zero offset seen anywhere in the torrent.\n\nThe value then feeds directly into the write offsets in `construct_file()`.\n\nCorrect form is an explicit `is None` check, computed from this file's own global start offset.","files":null}]}